/*
:name: spec_calls_gate_single_pin
:type: comptime
:verifier_pass: 2
:verifier_fail: 0
*/

// docs 06b-instantiation.md "Basic gates": "A basic gate is an ordinary call:
// every argument is named with the cell's LGraph pin name, unless a call naming
// exception applies (a single-pin gate may take its value unnamed)".
// qa.md Appendix §8: "... unless a call naming exception applies".
// `__not` has the single pin `a` (graph/cell.cpp), so exception 1 (a single
// parameter) lets its operand be unnamed.

cassert(__not(0) == -1)
cassert(__not(0xff) == -256)
